# openOODA Master 100-Subsystem Architectural Ledger
File: openOODA/docs/audit-history/2026-11-06-subsystem-ledger.oot

Provenance: converted from openOODA/docs/audit-history/2026-11-06-subsystem-ledger.md
(166 lines). All 100 subsystem rows, the four mandatory invariants, and the audit warning
are preserved. Only the header, this note, and the prose line wrapping changed.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> Every subsystem in this unified ledger is governed by **four mandatory invariants**:
> 1. **Explicit `CapReg64` Authority**: Imports
>    [`capreg.oo`](file:///Projects/openOODA-core/std/sec/capreg.oo) and validates domain
>    capability bits (`oo_cap_reg64_check` / `oo_cap_bit_index`) fail-closed
>    (`0` ambient authority).
> 2. **Post-Quantum Sealing**: Imports
>    [`pqc.oo`](file:///Projects/openOODA-core/std/sec/pqc.oo) and seals every state
>    transition with `oo_pqc_sha3_round`.
> 3. **Zero Third-Party Brand / Trademarked Names**: All directory names, `.oo`
>    filenames, function symbols, and docstrings use pure, generic openOODA functional
>    names (`Name the function, not the brand`).
> 4. **Clean 6-Folder Root Hierarchy (`oovfs/layout/root_tree.oo`)**:
>    - `/system` — Immutable kernel, boot slots, hardware drivers, and content-addressed system packages
>    - `/apps` — Self-contained desktop and CLI application bundles
>    - `/users` — Isolated per-user home directories (`/users/<name>`)
>    - `/config` — Transactional system configuration hives and `CapReg64` security policies
>    - `/data` — Persistent system data, audit logs, object storage, and container layers
>    - `/run` — Ephemeral runtime sockets, zero-copy IPC channels, and capability-gated device nodes

> [!WARNING]
> **Audit 2026-11-06 03:35 HST (verified on disk):** All 95 linked module paths now
> resolve (32 stale paths corrected to their real renamed files). However, **25 modules
> marked "⚠️ no reg64 gate"** only fold `oo_cap_bit_index(...)` into the PQC hash — they
> do **not** call `oo_cap_reg64_check` and so do not fail closed on a missing/stale
> capability. Invariant #1 is not yet enforced for those rows. Commit hashes are each
> repo's HEAD at audit time, not necessarily the commit that introduced the module. Row
> #41 maps to `share_migrate.oo`, which does not clearly cover the QUIC-transport part
> of that row's title.

---

